From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:26:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Controller: transcode only the requested outputs

tcd decoded every packet and then encoded it into every codec, also when
the reflector needed only one of them. For software vocoders this costs
CPU on each 20 ms frame and adds latency, because the reply waits for
the slowest encoder.

Each packet now has a requested-outputs mask (see TCPacketDef.h):

- A v2 packet gives the mask in its frame header. 0 means all codecs,
  which is the upstream behaviour.
- A raw packet cannot give a mask. It gets the new tcd.ini key
  DefaultOutputs, which is "all" when it is not set. So a raw link works
  as before.

With the mask:

- When the only requested output is the input codec, tcd sends the
  reply at once, with no decode.
- Otherwise the input is decoded to audio once, and the audio goes only
  to the encoder queues of the requested outputs.
- The reply goes out when the requested fields are set.
- Every field that was not requested is zero in the reply, the input
  field too. The v2 reply header gives the mask of the filled fields.

CTranscoderPacket now zero-initializes its packet and audio, so no
uninitialized memory can go into a reply.

Note: codec2 3200 output puts two 20 ms frames in one m17 field, and
the odd frame takes its first half from the even frame. A reflector
that wants m17 output must request it for both frames of a pair.
Encoders and decoders keep state from frame to frame, so a stream must
keep the same mask for the best audio.
